Problem Statement:  
Develop a C++ program to find and display the inorder  
predecessor and successor of a specified node  
in a threaded binary search tree (BST).  
The program should build the threaded BST by inserting nodes,  
replace null child pointers with threads to inorder neighbours,  
and locate the given node.  
It should then display its predecessor and successor,  
wherever they exist, without using recursion or a stack.
